course: dictionary
lesson: 7058
title: Pat: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The Cat pats his cheek and tickles him with his tail, and the Baby laughs.» Here pat is an action: the cat touches the cheek gently, so pat is a verb.
explain: Pat can also be a thing. «A pat on the back» means praise, not a hit. Read it, then swap in your meaning: does «praise» make sense? Does a «pat of butter» mean a small flat piece? If yes, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Some phrases have a meaning of their own. «Have your times tables off pat» means you know them perfectly by heart. You cannot work that out from pat alone, so look at the whole phrase.
fact: To pat means to touch someone or something gently and quickly with your flat hand, several times.
fact: A pat is a light, gentle touch with your hand.
fact: A pat of butter is a small flat piece.
fact: «Off pat» means learned perfectly, known by heart.
fact: Before you pat a dog, ask the owner first and let the dog sniff your hand.
exercise: «The Cat pats his cheek and tickles him with his tail.» What does pats mean here? | *Touches gently with a flat hand | Hits hard with a stick | Cuts with scissors | Pushes away roughly
exercise: Mum says, «Give yourself a pat on the back for tidying up.» What does a pat on the back mean? | *Praise, to say well done | Turning round to walk away | A pat of butter | A hard smack
exercise: Which phrase means you know your times tables perfectly? | *Off pat | A pat of butter | Pat dry | Pat the dough
test: Sam says, «I patted my wet face dry with a towel.» What does pat dry mean? | Rub hard until it shines | *Dry with light, gentle touches, not rubbing | Put it in a warm oven | Soak it in water
test: In «Pat the lollipop lady says, Lovely weather for ducks, chuck!», what is Pat? | A pat of butter | *A person's name | A gentle touch | A way to dry something
exam: «He gave the puppy a pat and said, Good boy.» What does pat mean here? | Learned perfectly by heart | *A light, gentle touch | A hard hit | A small flat piece of butter
